            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis of α-keto imides through copper-catalyzed oxidation of N-sulfonyl ynamides.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10156-10159</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7ob02728a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A novel copper-catalyzed N-oxide oxidation of N-sulfonyl ynamides is disclosed. This non-noble metal-catalyzed protocol enables facile and efficient access to valuable α-keto imides in generally good to excellent yields. Other notable features of this method include widespread availability of the substrates, compatibility with broad functional groups, a simple procedure, mild conditions, and in particular, no need to exclude moisture or air (&quot;open flask&quot;).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
